description:
## Problem
Only DuckDB, ClickHouse and Snowflake have introspectors. Candidate introspectors from structured catalogs:
- Databricks `DESCRIBE DETAIL`;
- BigQuery `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS`;
- Redshift `SVV_TABLE_INFO` / `PG_TABLE_DEF`;
- PostgreSQL `pg_index` / `pg_partitioned_table`;
- StarRocks `information_schema.tables_config`;
- Trino / Iceberg `$properties` / `$partitions`;
- Firebolt `information_schema.indexes`;
- Synapse `sys.pdw_*`;
- MotherDuck `duckdb_indexes()`.

The published corpus has zero tuned bundles on any of these (244 bundles; 5 tuned, all DuckDB), and several render no layout at execution today. The re-review recommended scoping the binary verified gate to DuckDB and ClickHouse and presenting raw catalog facts elsewhere.

## Options
- **(A) Recommended.** Facts-only by default; add a full introspector per platform only on recorded demand.
- **(B)** An introspector per platform as each execution renderer lands.

## Guardrails
- No new introspector before this gate is done.
- Introspectors must be bounded (filter inside the SQL `WHERE`, truncation measured on the raw result), non-raising and structured-catalog only.
- An introspector lands only after that platform renders the layout at execution.

## Gate protocol
- This is a decision record, not an implementation.
- Implementation items that list this gate in `needs` must not start until it is done.
- The decision owner is the maintainer.
- Record the outcome as a dated ADR addendum (addenda only; do not rewrite recorded decisions) and paste the decision into this item's context before finishing.
